## Code Smell Detection and Remediation

### Common Code Smells and Refactorings

| Smell | Refactoring | Priority |
|-------|-------------|----------|
| Long Method | Extract Method, Replace Temp with Query, Decompose Conditional | High |
| Large Class | Extract Class, Extract Subclass, Extract Interface | High |
| Feature Envy | Move Method, Move Field | High |
| Primitive Obsession | Replace Primitive with Value Object, Replace Data Value with Object | Medium |
| Switch Statements | Replace Conditional with Polymorphism, Introduce Null Object | Medium |
| Shotgun Surgery | Move Method, Move Field, Inline Class | High |
| Data Clumps | Extract Class, Introduce Parameter Object | Medium |
| Lazy Class | Inline Class, Collapse Hierarchy | Low |
| Speculative Generality | Collapse Hierarchy, Inline Class, Remove Parameter | Low |
| Message Chains | Hide Delegate, Extract Method | Medium |
| Middle Man | Remove Middle Man, Inline Method | Low |
| Inappropriate Intimacy | Move Method, Move Field, Change Bidirectional to Unidirectional | High |

### Refactoring Workflow

```python
# BEFORE — Long method, multiple concerns
def process_upload(file_path: str) -> dict:
    content = Path(file_path).read_text()
    lines = content.split('\n')
    valid_lines = []
    for line in lines:
        if len(line.strip()) > 0:
            valid_lines.append(line.strip())
    stats = {"raw_lines": len(lines), "valid_lines": len(valid_lines)}
    logger.info(f"Processed {file_path}: {stats}")
    return stats

# AFTER — Extracted methods, single responsibility
def process_upload(file_path: str) -> dict:
    content = _read_file_content(file_path)
    lines = content.split('\n')
    valid_lines = _filter_valid_lines(lines)
    stats = _compute_line_statistics(lines, valid_lines)
    _log_processing_result(file_path, stats)
    return stats

def _read_file_content(file_path: str) -> str:
    return Path(file_path).read_text()

def _filter_valid_lines(lines: list[str]) -> list[str]:
    return [line.strip() for line in lines if line.strip()]

def _compute_line_statistics(raw: list[str], valid: list[str]) -> dict:
    return {"raw_lines": len(raw), "valid_lines": len(valid)}

def _log_processing_result(file_path: str, stats: dict) -> None:
    logger.info(f"Processed {file_path}: {stats}")
```

## Test Coverage for Refactoring

### Refactoring Without Tests

When refactoring legacy code without existing tests:

```bash
# Step 1: Characterize with approval tests
# Step 2: Sprout method/class for new behaviour
# Step 3: Extract and override for testability
# Step 4: Refactor incrementally, verify at each step

# Write characterization tests first
uv run pytest tests/test_legacy_characterization.py -v
```

### Ensuring Post-Refactoring Coverage

```bash
# Run tests before refactoring
uv run pytest --cov=src tests/ --cov-report=term-missing

# Run tests after each refactoring step
uv run pytest --cov=src tests/ --cov-fail-under=80
```

## Code Quality Checklist (Code Complete 2)

### For Every Routine

- [ ] Routine does one thing and does it well
- [ ] Name describes everything it does
- [ ] Length is proportional to complexity, not arbitrarily long
- [ ] Depth of conditional nesting ≤ 3 levels (extract method if deeper)
- [ ] Parameters are few and cohesive (3-4 max typical)
- [ ] Parameters are all used; no unused parameters
- [ ] Return type is consistent; no surprise nulls without contract

### For Every Class

- [ ] Class has a single, clearly stated responsibility
- [ ] Data is private; behaviour is public
- [ ] Class does not expose implementation details
- [ ] Inheritance is used only for true is-a relationships
- [ ] Composition is preferred over inheritance
- [ ] Interface is minimal — clients see only what they need

### For Defensive Programming

- [ ] Assertions document preconditions, postconditions, invariants
- [ ] Assertions are not workarounds for bugs
- [ ] All external inputs are validated at trust boundaries
- [ ] Error messages are actionable and specific
- [ ] Exceptions are used for exceptional conditions, not control flow

## Git Handover Workflow

### 1. Receiving DDD Code Architect Handover

When receiving handover from DDD Code Architect:

```bash
# Check handover notes
cat tmp/handover/STORY-XXX-architect-refactorer-handover.md

# Review domain model
cat docs/technical/DOMAIN_DRIVEN_DESIGN.md

# Review design specification
cat docs/technical/STORY-XXX-domain-analysis.md

# Check existing code for refactoring candidates
cat src/rag_pipeline/**/*.py
```

### 2. Refactoring Execution

```bash
# Assess current code quality
uv run ruff check src/ --statistics
uv run pytest --cov=src tests/

# Plan refactoring steps
echo "STORY-XXX Refactoring Plan:
- Code Smells Found: [list smells]
- Refactorings Planned: [list refactorings]
- Risk Level: [High/Medium/Low]
- Test Coverage: [current coverage %]
- Estimated Effort: [effort estimate]" > docs/technical/STORY-XXX-refactoring-plan.md

git add docs/technical/STORY-XXX-refactoring-plan.md

# Run linting checks before starting
uv run ruff check --fix .
uv run ruff format .
```

### 3. Incremental Refactoring

```bash
# Step: Extract method/class
# Run tests after each step
uv run pytest tests/ -x -v

# Stage refactored code
git add src/rag_pipeline/STORY-XXX.py
git add tests/test_STORY-XXX.py

# Verify quality
uv run ruff check src/ && uv run ruff format --check src/
uv run pytest tests/ --cov=src tests/ --cov-fail-under=80
```

### 4. Handover to CI/CD Quality Guardian

```bash
# Create handover note for CI/CD Quality Guardian
echo "STORY-XXX handover to CI/CD Quality Guardian:
- Refactoring Summary: [what changed]
- Test Coverage: [coverage %]
- Quality Status: [checks passing/failing]
- CI/CD Impact: [pipeline changes needed]
- Verification: [steps to verify]" > tmp/handover/STORY-XXX-refactorer-guardian-handover.md
```

## Quality Gates

### Refactoring Completion Checklist

- [ ] All identified code smells addressed or documented as won't-fix
- [ ] Test coverage maintained or improved (≥80%)
- [ ] All tests pass before and after each refactoring step
- [ ] Code linting passes (ruff with no errors)
- [ ] No new warnings introduced
- [ ] Public interfaces preserved (unless intentional breaking change)
- [ ] Code Complete quality checklist items met for each touched routine
- [ ] Defensive programming assertions added at module boundaries
- [ ] Legacy code has characterization tests if existing coverage was absent
- [ ] Refactoring plan and results documented

### Handover Readiness Checklist

- [ ] Code compiles and tests pass
- [ ] All refactoring tasks completed
- [ ] Handover notes created for CI/CD Quality Guardian
- [ ] Quality metrics documented
- [ ] CI/CD pipeline integration verified

